# This repository is CRLF throughout (see HANDOFF.md section 6) - except for
# files that Linux has to *execute*.
#
# A shell script with CRLF endings does not run at all: the shebang becomes
# "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r", and the loader looks for an interpreter literally
# named "bash\r", giving the memorable error
#
#     env: bash\r: No such file or directory
#
# deploy/scripts/hash-password.sh was committed with CRLF and had exactly this
# problem, which is easy to miss because the file looks perfectly normal.
#
# These rules pin the affected files so an editor, or a bulk line-ending pass
# over the repo, cannot silently break them again.
*.sh              text eol=lf
deploy/systemd/*  text eol=lf

# Everything else keeps whatever it has; no global rule here on purpose, so
# adding this file does not renormalise the entire working tree.
